The bug occurs because there is no null check for the `value` parameter retrieved from `helper.getParameter(option.name())`. If `value` is null, the subsequent call to `option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value)` will lead to a null pointer exception or incorrect behavior when processing single-choice parameters like SUBJECT or DEPARTMENT.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (value != null) {
    Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a null check for the `value` parameter before attempting to look it up. This prevents the code from trying to process a null value, thereby avoiding exceptions and ensuring that the export functionality works correctly for single-choice parameters.

